#| msgid ""
#| "</details>\n"
#| "You can run your Qiskit primitive workloads using REST APIs in one of three execution modes, depending on your needs: job, session, and batch. This topic explains these modes.\n"
msgid ""
"</details>\n"
"You can run your IBM Quantum primitive workloads using REST APIs in one of three execution modes, depending on your needs: job, session, and batch. This topic explains these modes.\n"
msgstr ""
"</details>\n"
"Anda boleh menjalankan beban kerja primitif Qiskit menggunakan REST API dalam salah satu daripada tiga mod pelaksanaan, bergantung pada keperluan anda: job, session, dan batch. Topik ini menerangkan mod-mod tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
#| "This documentation utilizes the Python `requests` module to demonstrate the Qiskit Runtime REST API. However, this workflow can be executed using any language or framework that supports working with REST APIs. Refer to the [API reference documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/tags/jobs) for details.\n"
#| "</Admonition>\n"
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"This documentation utilizes the Python `requests` module to demonstrate the IBM Quantum Compute Service REST API. However, this workflow can be executed using any language or framework that supports working with REST APIs. Refer to the [API reference documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest) for details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Dokumentasi ini menggunakan modul Python `requests` untuk menunjukkan REST API Qiskit Runtime. Walau bagaimanapun, aliran kerja ini boleh dilaksanakan menggunakan mana-mana bahasa atau rangka kerja yang menyokong kerja dengan REST API. Rujuk [dokumentasi rujukan API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/tags/jobs) untuk butiran lanjut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job mode with REST API {#job-mode-with-rest-api}"
msgstr "Mod job dengan REST API {#job-mode-with-rest-api}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In job mode, a single primitive request of Estimator or Sampler is made without a context manager. See how to run a quantum circuit using [Estimator](/guides/estimator-rest-api) and [Sampler](/guides/sampler-rest-api) for some examples.\n"
msgstr "Dalam mod job, satu permintaan primitif tunggal daripada Estimator atau Sampler dibuat tanpa pengurus konteks. Lihat cara menjalankan litar kuantum menggunakan [Estimator](/guides/estimator-rest-api) dan [Sampler](/guides/sampler-rest-api) untuk beberapa contoh.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session mode with REST API {#session-mode-with-rest-api}"
msgstr "Mod session dengan REST API {#session-mode-with-rest-api}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "A session is a Qiskit Runtime feature that lets you efficiently run multi-job iterative workloads on quantum computers. Using sessions helps avoid delays caused by queuing each job separately, which can be particularly useful for iterative tasks that require frequent communication between classical and quantum resources. More details about Sessions can be found in the [documentation](/guides/execution-modes).\n"
msgid "A session is a feature that lets you efficiently run multi-job iterative workloads on quantum computers. Using sessions helps avoid delays caused by queuing each job separately, which can be particularly useful for iterative tasks that require frequent communication between classical and quantum resources. More details about Sessions can be found in the [documentation](/guides/execution-modes).\n"
msgstr "Session ialah ciri Qiskit Runtime yang membolehkan anda menjalankan beban kerja berbilang job secara berulang pada komputer kuantum dengan cekap. Menggunakan session membantu mengelakkan kelewatan akibat baris gilir setiap job secara berasingan, yang amat berguna untuk tugas berulang yang memerlukan komunikasi kerap antara sumber klasik dan kuantum. Butiran lanjut tentang Session boleh didapati dalam [dokumentasi](/guides/execution-modes).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Open Plan users cannot submit session jobs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Pengguna Open Plan tidak boleh menghantar job session.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start a session {#start-a-session}"
msgstr "Mulakan session {#start-a-session}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Begin by creating a session and obtaining a session ID.\n"
msgstr "Mulakan dengan mencipta session dan mendapatkan ID session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output\n"
msgstr "Output\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Close a session {#close-a-session}"
msgstr "Tutup session {#close-a-session}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is good practice to close a `Session` when all jobs are done. This will reduce wait time for subsequent users.\n"
msgstr "Adalah amalan yang baik untuk menutup `Session` apabila semua job selesai. Ini akan mengurangkan masa menunggu bagi pengguna berikutnya.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch mode with REST API {#batch-mode-with-rest-api}"
msgstr "Mod batch dengan REST API {#batch-mode-with-rest-api}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, you can submit a batch job by specifying the `mode` in the request payload. Batch mode can help shorten processing time if all jobs can be provided at the outset. Learn about batch mode in the [introduction to execution modes](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode) guide.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif, anda boleh menghantar job batch dengan menentukan `mode` dalam muatan permintaan. Mod batch boleh membantu memendekkan masa pemprosesan jika semua job boleh diberikan sekaligus. Ketahui lebih lanjut tentang mod batch dalam panduan [pengenalan kepada mod pelaksanaan](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples of jobs submitted in a session {#examples-of-jobs-submitted-in-a-session}"
msgstr "Contoh job yang dihantar dalam session {#examples-of-jobs-submitted-in-a-session}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once a session is set up, one or more Sampler or Estimator jobs can be submitted to the same session by specifying the session ID.\n"
msgstr "Setelah session ditetapkan, satu atau lebih job Sampler atau Estimator boleh dihantar ke session yang sama dengan menentukan ID session.\n"

